  bootwright / preflight
      Check, without changing anything, whether the selected context is ready for the stages
      apply runs, in one report. controller checks the controller host's prerequisites, the
      target tools this context's controller stage selects and its host binding;
      infrastructure-services checks the firewall admission of the controller's managed service
      sockets; substrates checks the capacity of the hosts that hold the context's Machines;
      machines has no checks; clusters checks the OpenShiftClusters and CephClusters that
      --clusters selects, or all of them. add-ons has no checks yet and is refused. It reports
      only what it observes: external services, a Registry or LoadBalancer and managed services
      on other Machines are not checked, and apply checks them itself. The SSH and
      observe-host-keys options apply to the CephCluster checks. --dry-run runs no process and
      reports every check pending. For the controller host alone, before any context exists,
      run controller check.

  Usage
    bootwright preflight [flags]

  Command flags
      --clusters           Select comma-separated cluster names (default: all)
      --dry-run            Limit work to the command's dry-run boundary
      --observe-host-keys  Observe unknown SSH keys without accepting them · default true
      --stage              Select comma-separated stages to check (default: every stage but
                           add-ons) (values: controller, infrastructure-services, substrates,
                           machines, clusters, add-ons)

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright preflight --context lab --stage controller,substrates
